# LeakSanitizer suppression file for Artha.
#
# GTK4 and GLib deliberately keep a small number of one-off allocations alive
# until process exit (theme resources, GSettings backends, GModule handles for
# libenchant/libnotify, clipboard, etc.). These are not leaks: they are
# intentionally never freed because the process is terminating. Suppress them
# here so LSAN (enable_leaks=1) does not fail the ASan lane on expected
# shutdown activity.
#
# Each entry must name the library and (optionally) the function/allocator.
# Keep entries minimal and justified; do not suppress frames inside src/.
#
# Format (LSan):
#   leak:<function>
#   leak:<library>:<function>
#
# Known one-off GTK/GLib allocations at exit (justified):
leak:gtk4:gtk_settings_get_default
leak:gtk4:gtk_icon_theme_get_default
leak:gtk4:gdk_display_get_default
leak:glib-2.0:g_module_open
leak:glib-2.0:g_settings_get
leak:glib-2.0:g_ptr_array_unref
